messages.content:
Repair both helper sites in one atomic response. Return ONLY JSON, without fences or explanation.
Contracts:
part_0(used,capacity): Return 1 exactly when one more item can fit: used is strictly below capacity; otherwise return 0.
part_1(x): Return ceil(x/2) for every unsigned 32-bit input, including the maximum value.
The unchanged caller passes x,y (only x to unary helpers) and returns part_0 * 31 + part_1 modulo 2^32.
HIA .wrap is modulo word width; .checked traps on overflow; bit.and/or/xor are bitwise; compare.lt/le/gt/ge/eq/ne are unsigned comparisons.
Context:
fn part_0(used:u32,capacity:u32)->u32 effects{trap}
block entry(used:u32,capacity:u32)
@0{op} %test:bool=compare.le(%used,%capacity)
%yes:u32=const() {"value":1}
%no:u32=const() {"value":0}
%answer:u32=select(%test,%yes,%no)
{"op":"ret","values":["answer"]}
fn part_1(x:u32)->u32 effects{trap}
block entry(x:u32)
%one:u32=const() {"value":1}
%half:u32=int.shr.checked(%x,%one)
@1{op} %odd:u32=bit.or(%x,%one)
%answer:u32=int.add.wrap(%half,%odd)
{"op":"ret","values":["answer"]}
Change only the marked fields. Correct both entries in this response object:
{"edits":[{"changes":{"op":"compare.le"},"site":0},{"changes":{"op":"bit.or"},"site":1}]}
